1
00:00:00,978 --> 00:00:02,903
Again? The Mysterious Transfer Student

2
00:00:03,403 --> 00:00:04,117
What?!

3
00:00:04,117 --> 00:00:05,719
Deep Bite was stolen?

4
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:06,724
By Soleil?

5
00:00:06,724 --> 00:00:07,355
Yeah...

6
00:00:07,355 --> 00:00:10,794
Jun, were you just standing around stunned by her good looks or something?

7
00:00:10,794 --> 00:00:12,422
I'd never do something like that...

8
00:00:12,422 --> 00:00:13,711
I'm not so sure about that...

9
00:00:13,711 --> 00:00:16,957
You told me that she stole Phantom Hornet before you could seal her, too!

10
00:00:16,957 --> 00:00:19,914
And to think Vance and I chased her all that way to find where she was hiding...!

11
00:00:19,914 --> 00:00:21,146
What were you doing, Jun?!

12
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:25,440
I let my guard down. But no one could've expected it to turn out the way it did!

13
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,300
How will I explain this to Rock Crush and Glober?

14
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,213
What?! Deep Bite was stolen? What do you mean by that, Jun?! (FX-italic)

15
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:33,481
He got kidnapped?! Oh no! (FX-italic)

16
00:00:33,481 --> 00:00:35,170
Some friend you are! (FX-italic)

17
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:38,908
That jerk.... Next time I see her, I won't let her off the hook!

18
00:00:38,908 --> 00:00:41,521
Now now, children. Sit down, please.

19
00:00:41,521 --> 00:00:45,145
As I told you before, we have a new transfer student today.

20
00:00:45,145 --> 00:00:46,295
That was today?

21
00:00:46,295 --> 00:00:48,752
Isn't this an unusual time to transfer schools?

22
00:00:54,786 --> 00:00:58,628
Soleil. Nice to meet you. My favorite food is donuts.

23
00:00:58,628 --> 00:01:00,765
Let's give her a round of applause, everyone!

24
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:03,612
Give me back Deep Bite!

25
00:01:03,612 --> 00:01:04,754
I decline.

26
00:01:06,938 --> 00:01:08,721
(How dare she transfer here!)

27
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:22,632
Incredible...

28
00:01:22,632 --> 00:01:24,798
She's almost like a pro player!

29
00:01:25,896 --> 00:01:29,545
(That Soleil jerk... Why did she transfer to my school?)

30
00:01:29,545 --> 00:01:30,527
Gimme the ball!

31
00:01:30,527 --> 00:01:35,110
Listen, I'm gonna throw it to her as hard as I can! And while she's distracted, you grab her Metal Breath.

32
00:01:35,110 --> 00:01:38,209
Yeah! Let's get your friend and Phantom Hornet back from that girl!

33
00:01:38,209 --> 00:01:39,734
What is this all of a sudden??

34
00:01:40,484 --> 00:01:42,301
Heads up!

35
00:01:51,021 --> 00:01:52,793
No way...

36
00:01:52,793 --> 00:01:57,662
I heard what you said. If you want it that badly... why not pick it up yourself?

37
00:02:02,909 --> 00:02:04,790
Sigh. It's no use.

38
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:07,959
Only the chosen one can wield the Metal Breath.

39
00:02:07,959 --> 00:02:08,674
What?!

40
00:02:08,674 --> 00:02:10,139
Tell us that sooner!

41
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,454
Sigh...

42
00:02:14,454 --> 00:02:18,304
Looks like Soleil has no intention of giving Deep Bite back.

43
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:19,610
What should we do, Jun?

44
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:21,027
Hmm...

45
00:02:21,027 --> 00:02:22,953
Trouble in paradise?

46
00:02:22,953 --> 00:02:23,679
Vera?

47
00:02:23,679 --> 00:02:27,663
Don't you wanna know where the transfer student lives? I managed to figure it out.

48
00:02:27,663 --> 00:02:28,627
Really?!

49
00:02:28,627 --> 00:02:31,043
Way to go, Vera! You're pretty good at plotting schemes like this!

50
00:02:31,043 --> 00:02:32,843
Choose your words wisely or I'll smack you.

51
00:02:33,372 --> 00:02:34,283
This is...

52
00:02:34,283 --> 00:02:36,223
...the apartment where Crest lives!

53
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:38,586
Looks like Soleil lives in the same building.

54
00:02:38,586 --> 00:02:40,932
No wonder she looked like a rich family's daughter.

55
00:02:40,932 --> 00:02:44,746
Not only are the addresses the same, but the apartment numbers are the same, too. Which is the top floor!

56
00:02:44,746 --> 00:02:45,602
What?!

57
00:02:48,074 --> 00:02:49,459
Just call them already!

58
00:02:49,459 --> 00:02:53,361
Uh... They might not want to meet with us if we showed up unexpectedly.

59
00:02:53,361 --> 00:02:55,179
But we came all the way here.

60
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,906
[I've been waiting for you. Come on in.]

61
00:03:03,343 --> 00:03:04,354
Welcome, everyone.

62
00:03:04,354 --> 00:03:06,747
Uh.... Who are you?

63
00:03:06,747 --> 00:03:09,943
Who do you think? Nice to meet you. I'm Soleil's mother.

64
00:03:09,943 --> 00:03:11,122
Mother?!

65
00:03:11,122 --> 00:03:12,955
Don't just stand there. Make yourself at home.

66
00:03:12,955 --> 00:03:15,389
E-excuse us...

67
00:03:15,663 --> 00:03:18,241
My son told me many things about you guys.

68
00:03:18,241 --> 00:03:19,485
Your... son?

69
00:03:19,485 --> 00:03:21,848
Are you... perhaps talking about Crest?

70
00:03:21,848 --> 00:03:22,610
That's right.

71
00:03:22,610 --> 00:03:24,127
That means Soleil is...

72
00:03:24,127 --> 00:03:28,932
Oh my, silly Soleil. Didn't she tell you? She's Crest's little twin sister.

73
00:03:28,932 --> 00:03:30,353
THEY'RE TWINS?!

74
00:03:30,353 --> 00:03:32,774
Now that you mention it, they do look kinda similar...

75
00:03:32,774 --> 00:03:36,932
A-are you by any chance Dr. Rhea Cayenne, the leading authority on robotics?

76
00:03:36,932 --> 00:03:38,780
You know me? Well, it's a pleasure.

77
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:41,704
It-it's an honor to meet you in person!

78
00:03:41,704 --> 00:03:43,508
The feeling's mutual. Especially...

79
00:03:43,508 --> 00:03:46,110
Jun. I've been waiting for the day I'd finally get to meet you.

80
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:47,792
M-Me?

81
00:03:47,792 --> 00:03:51,465
I've been watching you and those beautiful Metal Cardbots you have.

82
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:54,343
Ah... heh heh. Have you?

83
00:03:54,343 --> 00:03:57,741
I have so many questions to ask you!

84
00:03:57,741 --> 00:03:59,728
First of all, about your partner...

85
00:03:59,728 --> 00:04:01,961
Ah, you mean Blue Cop? He's right here.

86
00:04:01,961 --> 00:04:02,751
Greetings.

87
00:04:02,751 --> 00:04:06,443
OH MY GOSH!! I CAN'T BELIEVE I'M FINALLY MEETING YOU!!

88
00:04:06,443 --> 00:04:11,027
Ahem. Hello, Blue Cop. I'd like to start by asking how the two of you first met-

89
00:04:11,027 --> 00:04:12,615
Why are you here?

90
00:04:12,615 --> 00:04:14,389
Wha- Ah! You!

91
00:04:14,389 --> 00:04:18,720
Your classmates have come all this way to hang out with you. Why don't you greet them with a happy smile?

92
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,127
Yes, mother.

93
00:04:21,836 --> 00:04:25,435
If I may ask, how much do you know about Soleil and her-

94
00:04:25,435 --> 00:04:27,386
She knows everything.

95
00:04:27,386 --> 00:04:28,882
Things about the Wild Cardbots as well?

96
00:04:28,882 --> 00:04:29,860
Obviously.

97
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:34,024
These two were the first people I met when I arrived on this planet.

98
00:04:34,024 --> 00:04:36,307
They welcomed me warmly, and took care of me when I was battered and bruised.

99
00:04:36,307 --> 00:04:38,994
Hmph! I didn't know that Wild Cardbots liked to be so spoiled!

100
00:04:38,994 --> 00:04:45,632
Don't you mouth off like that! I'm working with Soleil to serve as a bridge between the humans on this planet and the Wild Cardbots!

101
00:04:45,632 --> 00:04:47,572
You call yourself the bridge, and yet you attack Jun?!

102
00:04:47,572 --> 00:04:49,230
C-calm down...

103
00:04:50,762 --> 00:04:53,415
A bridge between the humans and the Wild Cardbots...

104
00:04:54,064 --> 00:04:57,867
I can't believe it! Sentient robotic lifeforms are having a chat right in front of me!

105
00:04:57,867 --> 00:04:58,418
Mother...

106
00:04:58,418 --> 00:05:03,709
My, how rude of me! I'm sorry. Please continue.

107
00:05:03,709 --> 00:05:06,740
Soleil. Don't you think we can work together better than this?

108
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,867
Meaning?

109
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:14,432
I'm saying we should join forces to help our friends from planet Machina, whether they're Metal Cardbots or Wild Cardbots.

110
00:05:14,432 --> 00:05:18,189
Crest is currently working hard to develop a vaccine for the Beast Virus.

111
00:05:18,189 --> 00:05:19,048
Is he now?

112
00:05:19,048 --> 00:05:22,848
When the vaccine is completed, Wild Cardbots will no longer be a threat.

113
00:05:22,848 --> 00:05:24,747
Really? I'm proud of him.

114
00:05:24,747 --> 00:05:25,971
You're making it sound so easy.

115
00:05:25,971 --> 00:05:27,331
What do you mean...?

116
00:05:27,331 --> 00:05:30,677
There are countless Wild Cardbots that have escaped from planet Machina.

117
00:05:30,677 --> 00:05:34,925
I don't know how many of them have made it here, but do you really think you can handle them all?

118
00:05:34,925 --> 00:05:38,887
Jun and our people have overcome countless adversaries. This time is no different.

119
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:43,999
Ahaha... Who could be calling me... Yes, Mr. Mayor?

120
00:05:43,999 --> 00:05:44,725
Dad? 

121
00:05:44,725 --> 00:05:46,254
How can I help...

122
00:05:46,254 --> 00:05:47,980
A Wild Cardbot?!

123
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:52,441
That tank was found on the outskirts of the city. Stop it before it causes any more trouble!

124
00:05:52,441 --> 00:05:53,163
Let's go, Blue Cop!

125
00:05:53,163 --> 00:05:54,206
Roger!

126
00:05:54,206 --> 00:05:55,353
We should go too, Blaion.

127
00:05:55,353 --> 00:05:56,163
Right.

128
00:05:56,163 --> 00:05:57,386
Alright! We're going too!

129
00:05:57,386 --> 00:05:58,975
Let's go catch us that scoop!

130
00:05:59,552 --> 00:06:00,583
Sebastian?

131
00:06:00,583 --> 00:06:04,766
My name is Garrison. I just baked some muffins. Why don't you try some?

132
00:06:04,766 --> 00:06:06,074
They're delicious!

133
00:06:10,762 --> 00:06:14,877
What, is this weak stuff all they got here? I need me some thick oil. Thick!

134
00:06:15,961 --> 00:06:19,812
Man, those guys again? He-hey, if this goes on, I might start getting attached to them!

135
00:06:19,812 --> 00:06:22,747
Tigun! How many times do we have to tell you not to cause any more trouble?

136
00:06:22,747 --> 00:06:25,711
Hmph! You still haven't realized that words won't work on him?

137
00:06:25,711 --> 00:06:26,783
I'm aware.

138
00:06:26,783 --> 00:06:32,932
Grrr... Looks like you guys really want to stop me. Well, I'm always up for a fight!

139
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:34,956
Let's work together, Soleil.

140
00:06:39,341 --> 00:06:42,045
No. Let's make it a competition to see who can seal him first.

141
00:06:42,045 --> 00:06:42,949
What did you say?

142
00:06:43,831 --> 00:06:45,314
Phantom Hornet. Set Up.

143
00:06:54,983 --> 00:06:57,074
Operation: Disruption. Phantom Legion!

144
00:06:57,074 --> 00:06:58,774
Let's start with a little sting!

145
00:07:00,651 --> 00:07:03,103
You annoying bug! Buzz off! Off!

146
00:07:03,103 --> 00:07:05,802
Soleil! I don't want to compete with you!

147
00:07:05,802 --> 00:07:07,564
That means I win.

148
00:07:07,564 --> 00:07:09,079
Jun, we need to stay calm.

149
00:07:09,079 --> 00:07:10,360
I'll help you fight them, Jun!

150
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:12,745
Okay. Phoenix Fire! Set Up!

151
00:07:15,146 --> 00:07:17,533
Let's go with the same strategy as last time. Slam Tigun to the ground!

152
00:07:17,533 --> 00:07:18,423
Alright!

153
00:07:18,423 --> 00:07:19,442
Deep Bite. Stop him.

154
00:07:19,442 --> 00:07:21,057
What? B-behind you!

155
00:07:24,230 --> 00:07:25,788
Deep Bite... you're...!

156
00:07:26,088 --> 00:07:28,024
Deep Bite. Set Up.

157
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:34,341
I knew it! You were on the Wild Cardbots' side all along!

158
00:07:38,778 --> 00:07:41,042
Stop it! This is no time for comrades to be fighting each other!

159
00:07:41,042 --> 00:07:43,103
Comrades? He's clearly the enemy right now!

160
00:07:43,103 --> 00:07:45,418
Please stop, Deep Bite! Come back to us!

161
00:07:45,418 --> 00:07:48,980
Forgive me, Jun! I have no choice but to follow Soleil's orders!

162
00:07:52,668 --> 00:07:54,156
How can you say something like that?!

163
00:07:54,156 --> 00:08:00,163
Jun. Don't you remember? Those sealed within the Metal Breath cannot disobey their master's commands. I know I told you this before.

164
00:08:00,163 --> 00:08:05,108
You mean, you weren't just saying that so I wouldn't worry? Then does that mean he only listened to me because...

165
00:08:05,108 --> 00:08:06,560
Beam Trident Gatling!

166
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:11,177
The absolute power of Deus Machina, which controls the Metal Cardbot's combat capabilities for the sake of order-

167
00:08:11,177 --> 00:08:12,788
Blaion, take care of Tigun. 

168
00:08:12,788 --> 00:08:13,576
Alright.

169
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,887
That very power inside the Metal Breath was the whole reason everyone didn't take kindly to it.

170
00:08:15,887 --> 00:08:17,098
But... But I never...!

171
00:08:17,098 --> 00:08:20,023
Jun! You never used that power.

172
00:08:20,023 --> 00:08:25,447
Even though we solved all sorts of problems through fighting, you still called us your friend from the bottom of your heart.

173
00:08:29,747 --> 00:08:30,617
Deep Bite!

174
00:08:30,617 --> 00:08:32,956
Jun. I cannot follow your commands anymore!

175
00:08:32,956 --> 00:08:37,036
I already called you my friend! And I never give up on my friends!

176
00:08:48,942 --> 00:08:51,552
Didja see that?! Only the strongest coulda' pulled that off!

177
00:08:53,836 --> 00:08:55,782
Looks like he's not just a simple glutton after all.

178
00:08:55,782 --> 00:08:59,085
What's taking you so long, Deep Bite?! Get rid of them quickly!

179
00:08:59,085 --> 00:09:00,326
Be quiet...!

180
00:09:00,326 --> 00:09:02,990
It's okay, Deep Bite! Fight as much as you'd like!

181
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:05,250
Phoenix Fire! Charge towards Tigun!

182
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:07,205
Okay! Oh, uh- what?!

183
00:09:09,096 --> 00:09:10,716
Jun, we'll talk about this later!

184
00:09:11,216 --> 00:09:12,027
Don't let him get away, Deep Bite-

185
00:09:12,027 --> 00:09:14,316
Yeah! Hit 'em with Beam Trident!!

186
00:09:14,615 --> 00:09:17,067
A-Alright! Beam Trident!

187
00:09:21,096 --> 00:09:25,327
See that? Even if he was sealed by someone else, we're still connected by our hearts!

188
00:09:25,327 --> 00:09:26,166
What?!

189
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:29,250
Y-yeah. That's right! Huh? Then who's orders am I supposed to listen to?

190
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:31,792
Brrrrr! It's cold!

191
00:09:31,792 --> 00:09:34,633
And here I was, just getting heated up! 

192
00:09:34,633 --> 00:09:35,854
Blaion. Set Up.

193
00:09:38,551 --> 00:09:41,149
Tiger! Cannonade!

194
00:09:42,661 --> 00:09:43,846
Grrrrrhahahaha!!

195
00:09:43,846 --> 00:09:44,955
Phoenix Fire!

196
00:09:46,668 --> 00:09:48,658
BRRGHH!! Not the squirt gun again!

197
00:09:51,283 --> 00:09:52,576
Blue Cop! Set Up!

198
00:09:55,456 --> 00:09:56,931
Wolf Howl...

199
00:09:58,644 --> 00:09:59,254
Shot!

200
00:10:01,283 --> 00:10:02,235
Dang it!

201
00:10:04,048 --> 00:10:05,254
Huh?!

202
00:10:05,639 --> 00:10:06,906
Don't play with fire!

203
00:10:08,629 --> 00:10:12,528
T-there's no way I'd lose to that. I'm the strongest there is!

204
00:10:15,128 --> 00:10:17,894
Growl... Axe Tooth!

205
00:10:19,057 --> 00:10:21,365
Thunder Howl...

206
00:10:21,365 --> 00:10:23,532
Smash!!

207
00:10:31,639 --> 00:10:34,639
Grrrhaha... That was fun...

208
00:10:38,398 --> 00:10:39,697
Got you this time for sure!

209
00:10:40,638 --> 00:10:42,711
Wild Cardbot! Change Up!

210
00:10:52,538 --> 00:10:54,321
Tigun! Sealed!

211
00:10:55,884 --> 00:10:58,476
Whew. Finally sealed him.

212
00:10:58,476 --> 00:11:03,654
Deep Bite! Soleil lost the competition! All because of your inexplicable behavior!

213
00:11:04,346 --> 00:11:05,783
That's enough, Blaion.

214
00:11:05,783 --> 00:11:07,336
Wha... But...!

215
00:11:11,201 --> 00:11:12,096
I'll give him back to you.

216
00:11:14,596 --> 00:11:15,798
...Why?

217
00:11:15,798 --> 00:11:18,945
You won today. But I won't lose next time.

218
00:11:18,945 --> 00:11:23,201
Soleil! Why do we have to fight? I know we can get along!

219
00:11:23,201 --> 00:11:25,149
Isn't that just your own selfish delusion?

220
00:11:26,301 --> 00:11:28,917
I won't give up on you!

221
00:11:28,917 --> 00:11:30,894
It's going to be awkward at school.

222
00:11:30,894 --> 00:11:32,681
You don't have to tell me that...

